---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NextSteps from "../components/NextSteps.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { pages } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="This site keeps nothing about you. What CF Gaming keeps on your Mac, and what it connects to."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy"
    lead="This site keeps nothing about you. CF Gaming keeps what it needs on your Mac: here's what, and what it connects to."
  />

  <div class="wrap stack">
    <section class="glass panel" aria-labelledby="site">
      <h2 id="site">This site</h2>
      <ul class="points">
        <li>No cookies, no analytics, no adverts, and nothing from other companies loaded into your browser.</li>
        <li>
          It's served by Cloudflare, which handles each visit to deliver the page, under <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          The download comes from GitHub, which counts each download, under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="glass panel" aria-labelledby="app">
      <h2 id="app">What CF Gaming keeps, on your Mac</h2>
      <ul class="points">
        <li>Your cases and their games, each case a folder of its own; Settings › About shows where.</li>
        <li>The people who play, with their colours and photos: CF Gaming keeps a small copy of each photo, on this Mac.</li>
        <li>
          Recordings, in Movies › CF Gaming unless you choose another folder. Only the game's window and sound are recorded,
          with voices if you turn them on, and only once macOS has allowed it.
        </li>
        <li>Its settings, and its logs, which say what went wrong when something doesn't start (Help › Show Logs).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>CF Gaming has no analytics: nothing in it counts or reports how you use it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="glass panel" aria-labelledby="connects">
      <h2 id="connects">What it connects to, and when</h2>
      <ul class="points">
        <li>
          <strong>Updates:</strong> once a day, CF Gaming looks for a new version on its GitHub page. Settings › Updates can
          turn that off.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What you set up:</strong> Steam's installer from Valve; RetroArch, its files and its cores from libretro;
          the other emulators from their makers; CF Gaming's own build of Mupen64Plus-Next from its GitHub page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>RetroArch's own files:</strong> Settings › RetroArch compares CF Gaming's copies with libretro's site when
          you open it, and downloads the ones that changed only when you ask.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Covers,</strong> only when you choose Download Covers…, from libretro-thumbnails, on libretro's server or
          on GitHub.
        </li>
        <li>Steam and your games connect as they would on a PC, under their own makers' policies.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">It never downloads BIOS files or games.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <NextSteps items={[pages.licences, pages.about]} />
</BaseLayout>
